WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:03.960
King Paimon is the demonic antagonist who
motivates all of the horrific events seen

00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:04.960
in Hereditary.

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:09.620
But the entity’s origin goes back to 1577,
where he’s mentioned in Pseudomonarchia

00:00:09.620 --> 00:00:14.240
Daemonum, a Latin grimoire, or instructional
book on summoning supernatural entities.

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:17.550
According to that text, Paimon started as
an angel where he had a great admiration for

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:19.740
Lucifer and became one of his followers.

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:23.520
When Lucifer was thrown out of Heaven for
his arrogance, his followers, including Paimon,

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:24.520
were banished.

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:28.010
The most detailed information about Paimon’s
lore comes from The Lesser Key of Solomon,

00:00:28.010 --> 00:00:30.610
a mid-17th century spellbook on demonology.

00:00:30.610 --> 00:00:34.910
The Lesser Key of Solomon contains info on
72 demons and how to summon them for personal

00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:35.910
gain.

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:40.510
Each demon can be classified as a Duke, Prince,
Marquise, Knight, President, Earl or in this

00:00:40.510 --> 00:00:41.620
case: King.

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:45.120
Each demon has a sigil, or magic symbol that
represents them, which according to Lesser

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:48.990
Key of Solomon, are to be made of a specific
metal, based on their classification.

00:00:48.990 --> 00:00:51.170
For Kings, the sigil is to be made of gold.

00:00:51.170 --> 00:00:54.820
In Hereditary, the stand-in for the Lesser
Key of Solomon is a book found in Ellen’s

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:58.500
possessions simply titled Invocations, and
in the text we can see bits and pieces of

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:00.329
the same information found in Lesser Key.

00:01:00.329 --> 00:01:03.320
This book actually references earlier writings
from “The Goetia”.

00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:06.609
It’s talking about “Ars Goetia”, one
of the five books that make up The Lesser

00:01:06.609 --> 00:01:07.609
Key of Solomon.

00:01:07.609 --> 00:01:10.880
Diving into the quickly glossed over details
of this book tells us everything we need to

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:15.759
know about King Paimon, and allows us to unlock
all of the secrets of Hereditary.

00:01:15.759 --> 00:01:19.434
To learn everything about King Paimon, stick
around to the end of this video.

00:01:19.434 --> 00:01:21.201
